  <Placemark>
   <name>Small Craft Advisory issued November 28 at 12:24PM CST until November 30 at 9:00AM CST by NWS New Orleans LA</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_minor</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...West winds 20 to 25 kt with gusts up to 30 kt. Waves of 3
to 5 feet in the sounds, lakes, and bays and seas 5 to 7 ft in
the open Gulf waters can be expected.

* WHERE...All of the sounds, lakes, and bays and portions of the
open Gulf waters east of the Mississippi River.

* WHEN...From 6 AM Sunday to 9 AM CST Monday.

* IMPACTS...Conditions will be hazardous to small craft.</Snippet>
   <ExtendedData>
    <Data name="ext_event">
     <value>Small Craft Advisory</value>
    </Data>
    <Data name="ext_severity">
     <value>Minor</value>
    </Data>
    <Data name="ext_urgency">
     <value>Expected</value>
    </Data>
    <Data name="ext_certainty">
     <value>Likely</value>
    </Data>
    <Data name="ext_effective">
     <value>2026-11-28T12:24:00-06:00</value>
    </Data>
    <Data name="ext_expires">
     <value>2026-11-29T02:30:00-06:00</value>
    </Data>
    <Data name="ext_areaDesc">
     <value>Lake Maurepas; Lake Pontchartrain; Mississippi Sound; Lake Salvador and Lake Cataouatche; Lake Borgne; Breton Sound; Chandeleur Sound; Terrebonne Bay; Barataria Bay; Coastal Waters from Boothville LA to Southwest Pass of the Mississippi River out 20 nm; Coastal waters from Pascagoula Mississippi to Stake Island out 20 NM; Coastal waters from Pascagoula Mississippi to Stake Island Louisiana out 20 to 60 NM</value>
    </Data>
    <Data name="ext_description">
     <value />
    </Data>
    <Data name="ext_instruction">
